<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see sun west, rain east.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see sun west, rain east.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Tuesday were forecast to see sunny skies in the west and rain in the east, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see mainly sunny skies with a 30 percent probability of precipitation late in the day and highs of 20 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see sunny skies and highs of 25 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see cloudy skies and showers with highs of 20 to 23 Celsius.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
